<title>USA: Dell cuts price of corporate desktop PCs.</title>
<headline>Dell cuts price of corporate desktop PCs.</headline>
<dateline>ROUND ROCK, Texas 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dell Computer Corp said Monday it had cut U.S. prices by up to 15 percent on its OptiPlex line of corporate desktop personal computers.</p>
<p>It said its OptiPlex GSL PC, with a 200 MHz Pentium chip and 32 megabytes of memory, will now list at $1,959, down from $2,299 previously.</p>
<p>Its high-end OptiPlex GXpro will sell for $4,952, down from $5,376.  </p>
<p>Dell sells its PCs by mail-order only.</p>
</text>
